Correction to the commit body: the wake lock DOES work in the site shell.
The body says the shell iframe does not allow screen-wake-lock. That is wrong. A same-origin
frame gets screen-wake-lock and clipboard-write by default (allowlist 'self'), so the shell
needs no allow change. The first test read the lexical 'wakeLock' through window and got
undefined. The later check, in the shell with the unchanged allow list:
  allow 'microphone; autoplay; downloads'
  after startMic(): micOn true, wakeLock true, type 'screen'
  after stopMic():  micOn false, wakeLock false
